cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RetainIQ: causal retention decisioning for small subscription businesses"
message: "If you use this software or the SubSim benchmark, please cite the paper below."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrashamJ17/PBL-Proj"
authors:
  - given-names: Prasham
    family-names: Jain
    affiliation: "Manipal University Jaipur"
  - given-names: Rishi
    family-names: Gupta
    affiliation: "Manipal University Jaipur"
abstract: >-
  Churn prediction is a commodity; retention decisioning under small-sample
  causal uncertainty is not. This repository contains SubSim, a subscription
  churn simulator calibrated to published SMB-SaaS benchmarks that emits exact
  individual-level ground-truth counterfactuals; benchmark harnesses for four
  real randomised controlled trials; a discrete-time competing-risks survival
  model; a hierarchical Bayesian CATE estimator with a money-denominated
  abstention rule; an offer-ladder optimiser; and a validated holdout
  incrementality estimator. The central result is that whether effect-based
  targeting pays is governed by corr(tau, propensity), the correlation between
  estimated treatment effect and estimated outcome propensity.
keywords:
  - uplift modelling
  - heterogeneous treatment effects
  - causal inference
  - customer retention
  - survival analysis
  - abstention
  - subscription business
